title: LPL and WM rehearsal feedback
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Rituximab:'' IgM ≥4,000 mg/dL is not an absolute contraindication requiring plasma exchange.
** Defer initial rituximab and/or consider prophylactic exchange; flare also occurs below this threshold.
* ''Zanubrutinib:'' Can respond promptly; suitable for fit patients too, not simply a frailty option.
** Select by treatment duration, urgency, comorbidities, interactions, adherence, and preference.
* ''Diagnosis:'' Surface IgM is phenotypic support, not the defining serum monoclonal IgM criterion.
** t(11;14) also occurs in mantle cell lymphoma; interpret within morphology and immunophenotype.
* ''Prognosis:'' MSS-WM applies to untreated symptomatic WM, not asymptomatic progression or treatment selection.
** Asymptomatic progression risk: marrow burden, IgM, β2-microglobulin, albumin.
* ''Hyperviscosity:'' Recognize mucosal bleeding, visual disturbance, and neurologic symptoms; do not await viscosity results.
** Defer red-cell transfusion before exchange when feasible.
** Retinal examination: suspected hyperviscosity or IgM ≥3,000 mg/dL.
* ''Safety gaps:'' Screen hepatitis B before anti-CD20 therapy; type confirmed amyloid deposits.
** BTK inhibitor interruption risks IgM rebound; distinguish rebound and rituximab flare from progression.

Sources: NCCN Waldenström Macroglobulinemia/Lymphoplasmacytic Lymphoma v1.2027 (August 11, 2026), WM/LPL-1–3,A,B(1–2),C; MS-4–8,11. ASH SAP 9th ed. (2025), ch.49, pp.636–637; [[ASPEN|https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7596850/]].
